-- title:
--   Two invariant elements generate J modulo (x)J and n
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a commutative Noetherian ring $R$, and let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $R$ in the sense of the project structure `FormalODModule`: a two-variable formal group law $F$ over $R$ that is commutative, together with series $\mathrm{act}(a)$ for $a$ in $\mathbb Z_{p^2}$ and a series $\varpi$, all of which are endomorphisms of $F$ in the formal sense, satisfying $\mathrm{act}(1)=\mathrm{id}$, multiplicativity and additivity of $\mathrm{act}$, $\varpi\circ\varpi=\mathrm{act}(p)$ and $\varpi\circ\mathrm{act}(a)=\mathrm{act}(\sigma a)\circ\varpi$ for the Frobenius $\sigma$. Let $J$ be an ideal of $R[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$ such that: $R[\![x_0,x_1]\!]/J$ is a finite $R$-module; there is $q$ with $x_i^{q}\in J$ for both $i$; every element of $J$ has zero constant term; and $J$ is the ideal spanned by its invariant elements, where $w$ is called invariant when $w\in J$ and $w(F(x,y))-w(x)$ lies in the ideal generated by the image of $J$ under $x_i\mapsto y_i$. Let $\mathfrak n$ be a maximal ideal of $R$. Then there exist two invariant elements $r_0,r_1$ such that for every $f\in J$ one can write $f-\bigl(\sum_j a_j r_j+\sum_i x_i b_i\bigr)$ with $a_j,b_i\in R[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$, $b_i\in J$, all of whose coefficients lie in $\mathfrak n$.
--
--   This is the counting step at a maximal ideal in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation package: reduction modulo $\mathfrak n$ to the residue field, where an invariantly generated such ideal is generated by two invariant elements, gives two invariant elements generating $J$ modulo $(x_0,x_1)J$ and $\mathfrak n$. It feeds the construction of a free two-element generating system for subgroup ideals of formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_exists_pair_invariant_forall_exists_coeff_sub_mem_of_isMaximal.lean

